# <type>(<scope>): <subject> (max 50-72 chars)
# |<----  Using a Maximum Of 50-72 Characters  ---->|

# Explain why this change is being made and what problem it solves.
# Include technical details, design decisions, and context.
# Wrap lines at ~72 characters.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Commit Type Rules:
#   feat:     A new feature or public API addition
#   fix:      A bug fix
#   docs:     Documentation only changes
#   style:    Formatting, missing semicolons, no code change
#   refactor: Refactoring code without changing behavior
#   perf:     Code change that improves performance
#   test:     Adding or updating tests
#   build:    Changes to build system or dependencies
#   ci:       CI configuration and scripts
#   chore:    Maintenance tasks, tooling updates
#
# Scope Examples:
#   matrix, types, indexing, arithmetic, linalg, deps, ci
#
# Breaking Changes:
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description of breaking change>
#
# Issue References:
#   Closes #<issue-number>
#   Refs #<issue-number>
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
